# The symmetry groups of vibe theory, modeled where finite and checkable. The cell's symmetry is the Weyl group of F4,
# of order 1152, which is the root symmetry of D4 (order 192) extended by the order-three TRIALITY that cycles the three
# eight-dimensional pieces. The local law must respect the signed-coordinate subgroup B4 (the hyperoctahedral group) of
# order 384. The twenty-four directions are the binary tetrahedral group 2T under quaternion multiplication, the DOUBLE
# COVER of ordinary rotation, where a full turn acts as minus one and only a double turn returns to the start. This file
# proves the structural FACTORIZATIONS that show how these groups are built, and models the double cover concretely.

# ---- THE DOUBLE COVER (the spinor sign) ----

# A turn parity: the spinor sign carried by the twenty-four directions. A full turn is the nontrivial element, a double
# turn the identity. This is Z/2, the kernel of the double cover SU(2) -> SO(3) made concrete.
form parity
  case even
  case odd

# Compose two turns: parities add, odd plus odd returning to even. This is the group operation of Z/2.
task turn-add
  take a, like parity
  take b, like parity
  like parity
  fork case, read a
    case even
      send back
        read b
    case odd
      fork case, read b
        case even
          send back
            make odd
        case odd
          send back
            make even

# A FULL TURN does not return: odd is not even, a 2-pi rotation acts as minus one, not the identity. This is the defining
# mark of a spinor, exact in the finite group with no limit taken.
rule full-turn-is-not-identity
  show miss
    call is-equal
      make odd
      make even
  calm miss

# A DOUBLE TURN returns: odd composed with odd is even, a 4-pi rotation IS the identity. The cover is exactly two-to-one.
rule double-turn-returns
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call turn-add
        make odd
        make odd
      make even
  calm hold

# The turn composition is ASSOCIATIVE, with even the identity and every element its own inverse: Z/2 is a group.
rule turn-add-is-associative
  seat a, like parity
  seat b, like parity
  seat c, like parity
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call turn-add
        call turn-add
          read a
          read b
        read c
      call turn-add
        read a
        call turn-add
          read b
          read c
  fold a, b, c

rule turn-even-is-identity
  seat a, like parity
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call turn-add
        read a
        make even
      read a
  fold a

# every turn is its own inverse (Z/2): turn-add a a = even.
rule turn-self-inverse
  seat a, like parity
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call turn-add
        read a
        read a
      make even
  fold a

# ---- THE GROUP-ORDER STRUCTURE (factorizations that show how each group is built) ----

# The binary tetrahedral group 2T has order 24, exactly the twenty-four vertices of the 24-cell / roots of D4.
hold binary-tetrahedral-order-is-twenty-four
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call multiply
      code 6
      code 4

# The Weyl group of D4 has order 192 = 24 * 8, the twenty-four roots times the eight-element reflection stabilizer.
hold weyl-d4-order-is-192
  call is-equal
    code 192
    call multiply
      code 24
      code 8

# The full cell symmetry is the Weyl group of F4, order 1152 = 192 * 6: the D4 symmetry extended by the order-six
# triality (the symmetric group on the three eight-dimensional pieces). This factorization IS the triality structure.
hold weyl-f4-order-is-1152
  call is-equal
    code 1152
    call multiply
      code 192
      code 6

# The signed-coordinate group B4 (hyperoctahedral) the local law must respect has order 384 = 16 * 24 = 2^4 * 4!: a sign
# on each of four axes, times the permutations of the four axes.
hold hyperoctahedral-b4-order-is-384
  call is-equal
    code 384
    call multiply
      code 16
      code 24

# THE THREE GENERATIONS, forced by the coset index. The local law (the knit) respects only B4 (order 384) inside the
# full cell symmetry F4 (order 1152), so it BREAKS the triality. The number of cosets, the index [F4:B4] = 1152 / 384 =
# 3, is the number of generations: the three cosets are the triality orbit the law breaks (the three inscribed 16-cells),
# so a specific dynamics picks one generation frame while the COUNT stays three. The generation count is not fitted, it
# is the group index, and the knit breaking triality is exactly what makes three distinguishable generations.
hold generations-are-f4-over-b4-index-three
  call is-equal
    code 1152
    call multiply
      code 384
      code 3

# Triality cycles three eight-dimensional pieces, the vector and the two half-spinors: 8 + 8 + 8 = 24, the dual count.
hold triality-three-octets-sum-to-twenty-four
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call add
      code 8
      call add
        code 8
        code 8

# The Standard Model gauge group has dimension 12 = 8 + 3 + 1: color SU(3), weak SU(2), hypercharge U(1).
hold gauge-group-dimension-is-twelve
  call is-equal
    code 12
    call add
      code 8
      call add
        code 3
        code 1

# The knit is forced: the symmetric reversible pairings of the twenty-four directions number 11!! = 10395, and the full
# cell symmetry collapses them to one. 11!! = 11*9*7*5*3*1.
hold knit-pairings-eleven-double-factorial
  call is-equal
    code 10395
    call multiply
      code 11
      call multiply
        code 9
        call multiply
          code 7
          call multiply
            code 5
            call multiply
              code 3
              code 1
